<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28125" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δορῠφόρ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>body-guard:</i> used of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωφὰ
				πρόσωπα</span> or <i>mute characters</i> on the stage,
				<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				310c
			</span></i>: hence of Aridaeus, who was put up as the successor of
			Alexander, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ δέ, ὥσπερ ἐπὶ σκηνῆς δ., κωφὸν
					ἦν ὄνομα βασιλείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.791e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				77
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
